@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.portal"

Feature: Downloads Permissioning
	Testing the Permissioning of the Downloads portlet.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| DWNZENDWNZEN |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| DWNZENDWNZEN |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View dxp downloads as permissioned users
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	DXP downloads should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | DWNZENDWNZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	Then the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.3" product and "Product/Updates" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.3 Service Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.3" product and "Security Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.3 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible

Scenario: View portal downloads as permissioned users
	Portal downloads should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | DWNZENDWNZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	Then the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-10-15 Portal-171" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-06-25 Portal-170" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-12-17 Portal-71" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-08-21 Portal-70" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2015-12-17 Hotfix-1285" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2013-01-14 All-1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 5.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 5.2 EE SP5 Update 2011-02-24" should be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-10-15 Portal-171" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-06-25 Portal-170" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-12-17 Portal-71" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-08-21 Portal-70" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2015-12-17 Hotfix-1285" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2013-01-14 All-1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 5.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 5.2 EE SP5 Update 2011-02-24" should be visible

Scenario: View enterprise search downloads as permissioned users
	Enterprise search downloads should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | DWNZENDWNZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Enterprise Search - Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Enterprise Search"
	Then the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Enterprise Search" product and "Product" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.3" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.1" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.0" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Enterprise Search Standard" should not be visible
	And the download with the name "Elasticsearch 6 Downloads" should not be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Enterprise Search" product and "Product" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.3" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.1" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.0" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Enterprise Search Standard" should not be visible
	And the download with the name "Elasticsearch 6 Downloads" should not be visible

Scenario: View commerce downloads as permissioned users
	Commerce search downloads should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | DWNZENDWNZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Commerce Subscription Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dwnzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	Then the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Commerce" product and "Product" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Commerce 2.1.3" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Commerce 2.2.0" should be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Commerce" product and "Product" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Commerce 2.1.3" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Commerce 2.2.0" should be visible